<title>USA: Biodynamics settles litigation.</title>
<headline>Biodynamics settles litigation.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biodynamics International Inc said Wednesday it has settled litigation with the former owner of its German subsidiary.</p>
<p>It said the  settlement cancels a debt of $1.6 million Biodynamics owed to the former owner, which it did not identify.</p>
<p>The debt related to the original acqusition of the German subsidiary and its cancellation will result in an increase in equity, it said.</p>
<p>Biodeynamics is in the business of bioimplants for tissue repair.</p>
